    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Error Budget Accounting.</strong> You track how much reality can afford to wobble before it falls down.</p><ul><li>When you lead or advise a Tikkun-related experiment, ritual, or field test, you can declare an <em>error budget</em>.</li><li>Once per such operation, if the result would <strong>increase Darkness or corruption</strong> in a hex or Spark, the GM may reduce that increase by 1 (to a minimum determined by your campaign rules) as your mitigation and safety procedures kick in.</li><li>You cannot use this to erase catastrophic failures, but you can keep “oops” from becoming “we broke it forever.”</li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
